# `this.left.count`: what stands on the left is proven to be a Box or a Crate. A Box answers by a getter, a Crate by a field, so the read has no form over both. It is laid
# behind tests of the shape, outside of a loop too: the getter is called directly or copied in, the field is read out of its slot, and no read by name is left.
# f5 = weigh, f3 = the getter of Box, f6 = heavy
# RUN: walk f5 mechanisms=all-Inlining
# CHECK-LABEL: code f5:Body
# CHECK: = ShapeTest
# CHECK: = CallDirect {{*}} function=f3
# CHECK: = GetSlot {{*}} key="count"
# RUN(NONE): walk f5 mechanisms=all-Inlining
# NONE-LABEL: code f5:Body
# NONE-NOT: = PropGet {{*}} key="count"
# RUN(WITHHELD): walk f5 mechanisms=all-Inlining-Guesses
# WITHHELD-LABEL: code f5:Body
# WITHHELD: = PropGet {{*}} key="count"
# Two fields that lie in different slots are left to the read by name outside of a loop.
# RUN(FIELDS): walk f6 mechanisms=all-Inlining
# FIELDS-LABEL: code f6:Body
# FIELDS-NOT: = ShapeTest
# -- source: a-name-that-one-class-answers-by-a-getter-and-one-by-a-field-is-read-behind-tests-of-the-shape.ts
